        "original_id": "0d0bb950-5128-5042-916a-b8e78d398c40",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edsger Wybe Dijkstra\n- Roles: Dutch computer scientist, professor of mathematics, Schlumberger Centennial Chair in Computer Sciences\n- Organizations: University of Texas at Austin, Eindhoven University of Technology\n- Places: Eindhoven, Netherlands\n- Topics: computing science\n\nFacts:\n- Edsger Wybe Dijkstra was born on 11 May 1930 and died on 6 August 2002.\n- Edsger Wybe Dijkstra was a Dutch computer scientist and an early pioneer in many research areas of computing science.\n- Edsger Wybe Dijkstra was a professor of mathematics at Eindhoven University of Technology in Eindhoven, Netherlands, from 1962 to 1984.\n- Edsger Wybe Dijkstra held the Schlumberger Centennial Chair in Computer Sciences at the University of Texas at Austin from 1984 until his retirement due to ill health in 1999.",
